  "story": {
    "headline": "Rare turtle to be sent back home in 5,000-mile 'incredibly emotional' trip",
    "summary": "A rare turtle is being flown home to the Caribbean Sea after being found washed up in Wales.",
    "publisher": "Rally News",
    "url": "https://rally.news/categories/climate/?article=Rare%2Bturtle%2Bto%2Bbe%2Bsent%2Bback%2Bhome%2Bin%2B5%2C000-mile%2B%27incredibly%2Bemotional%27%2Btrip"
  },
  "researchBrief": "Rhossi, a critically endangered Kemp's Ridley sea turtle, was rescued from an Anglesey beach in December 2023. He was cold-stunned and near death, weighing less than one kilogram. After two years of rehabilitation at Anglesey Sea Zoo, Rhossi is now ready to be transported back to the Gulf of Mexico. The journey involves a helicopter ride to Heathrow, a cargo flight to Houston, and a final release into the Gulf of Mexico. The story is corroborated by multiple sources, including North Wales Live, nation.cymru, BBC Newsround, and North Wales Chronicle. The key details, such as the distance of the journey, the involvement of international conservation partners, and the critical status of Kemp's Ridley turtles, are consistently reported across these sources. The exact weight and size of Rhossi at the time of rescue are also verified. The story highlights the collaborative effort and the emotional significance of Rhossi's return to the wild.",
  "sources": [
    "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c62vd6j5llgo",
    "https://www.dailypost.co.uk/news/north-wales-news/critically-endangered-turtle-rescued-anglesey-34400577",
    "https://nation.cymru/news/critically-endangered-turtle-to-return-home-after-two-year-rehab-in-wales/",
    "https://www.northwaleschronicle.co.uk/news/26436783.rhossi-kemps-ridley-turtle-head-home-mexico/"
  ],
