    "pillar": "Climate & Environment",
    "headline": "Can a rescued turtle survive a 5,000-mile journey home? This little guy is about to find out.",
    "challenge": "Rhossi, a critically endangered Kemp's Ridley sea turtle, was found cold-stunned and near death on an Anglesey beach in December 2023. With only a slim chance of survival, his journey to recovery has been nothing short of miraculous.",
    "solution": "After two and a half years of dedicated care at Anglesey Sea Zoo, Rhossi is ready to embark on an epic 5,000-mile journey back to the Gulf of Mexico. A team of international conservationists, volunteers, and specialists are working together to make this happen.",
    "resultHeading": "Rhossi is heading home",
    "resultLine": "Follow his incredible journey and learn how you can support sea turtle conservation at the link in my bio.",
    "whyMatters": "Every healthy adult Kemp's Ridley turtle returned to the wild is a step toward strengthening the fragile population of this critically endangered species. Rhossi's story is a testament to the power of international collaboration and dedication to wildlife conservation.",
